r8169-dkms for Debian
=====================

This package installs the r8169 driver sources to /usr/src/r8169-<version>
and registers them with DKMS. DKMS builds the module for every installed
Proxmox 7.0 kernel from 7.0.14-22-pve on (BUILD_EXCLUSIVE_KERNEL and
BUILD_EXCLUSIVE_KERNEL_MIN in dkms.conf) and installs it to
/lib/modules/<kernel>/updates/dkms/, which takes precedence over the
in-tree module. The initramfs of each kernel that received the module is
regenerated, because r8169 is usually loaded from the initramfs.

Headers
-------

DKMS can only build for kernels whose headers are installed. Install
proxmox-default-headers (or proxmox-headers-<version> for a specific
kernel).

Checking which driver is in use
-------------------------------

  dkms status r8169
  modinfo -F filename r8169      # .../updates/dkms/r8169.ko*
  modinfo -F version r8169       # r8169-dkms package version
  modinfo -F upstream r8169      # kernel tag the sources come from
  cat /sys/module/r8169/version  # version of the loaded module

The in-tree r8169 has no version, so an empty /sys/module/r8169/version
means the in-tree driver is loaded. Reboot (or reload r8169 from a local
console) after installing the package.

Secure Boot
-----------

DKMS signs the module with its machine owner key
(/var/lib/dkms/mok.key, mok.pub). With Secure Boot enabled the key has to
be enrolled once:

  mokutil --import /var/lib/dkms/mok.pub

and confirmed in the MOK manager on the next boot.

Removing the package
--------------------

Removing the package deletes the DKMS module and regenerates the initramfs
of the affected kernels, so they boot with the in-tree r8169 again.

Conflicting packages
--------------------

Realtek's vendor drivers (r8168-dkms, realtek-r8125-dkms, ...) typically
blacklist r8169. Remove them, and any "blacklist r8169" line in
/etc/modprobe.d/, before using this package.
